  "term": "appeasement behavior",
  "definition": "Appeasement behavior is submissive signaling shown by a lower-status individual to indicate reduced willingness to escalate a conflict with a dominant opponent. In the source context, it is described as behavior that can lessen aggression and help stabilize social relationships.",
